# What the knowledge graph should not index.
#
# Gitignore syntax, and ADDITIVE to .gitignore — this can only exclude more,
# never re-include something .gitignore already dropped. So .venv/ and
# node_modules/ need no mention here; they are already out.

# The vendored engine.
#
# `upstream/` is a vendored copy of pynicotine, and it was HALF THE GRAPH —
# 3344 of 6662 nodes from 75 files, because a handful of protocol modules carry
# enormous symbol counts. That is not a cosmetic imbalance. Graph queries start
# from keywords, and pynicotine owns most of the vocabulary Seek also uses:
# search, connection, transfer, shares, user. Asking "how do search tabs share
# one sidecar connection" — a question about app/src/data/connectionStore.ts —
# returned forty nodes of Soulseek protocol code and never reached the file.
#
# Excluding it is safe because of the project's own non-negotiable: upstream
# stays unmodified, so it is read for reference and never edited. Reference
# lookups are a grep across 75 files, which is cheap. Having Seek's own 3283
# nodes be the whole graph is what makes the graph worth asking.
#
# To put it back: delete this line and run `graphify update .`
upstream/

